From 679392012b91766ad168c88156e7a39c2cfba067 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Oetken <patrick.oetken@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 15:47:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mavsdk_server: include <cstdint> for uint8_t

mavsdk_server.hpp uses uint8_t and uint32_t in setMavlinkIds() but relies
on another header to pull in <cstdint>. GCC 15's libstdc++ no longer does
that via <memory> or <string>, so the server fails to build:

  mavsdk_server.hpp: error: 'uint8_t' has not been declared

Refreshed for MAVSDK 4.1.0, where the header is
cpp/src/mavsdk_server/src/mavsdk_server.hpp (paths below are relative to
cpp/, the recipe's S).

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/mavsdk_server/src/mavsdk_server.hpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/mavsdk_server/src/mavsdk_server.hpp b/src/mavsdk_server/src/mavsdk_server.hpp
--- a/src/mavsdk_server/src/mavsdk_server.hpp
+++ b/src/mavsdk_server/src/mavsdk_server.hpp
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 #pragma once
 
+#include <cstdint>
 #include <memory>
 #include <string>
 
